{"name":"Intrigue","hex":"#635951","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"intrigue","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complicated or clandestine plot or scheme intended to effect some purpose by secret artifice; conspiracy; stratagem; the practice of engaging in hidden schemes.","Clandestine intercourse between persons; illicit intimacy; a liaison or affair."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To conceive or carry out a secret plan intended to harm; to form a plot or scheme.","To arouse the interest of; to fascinate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intrigue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Intrigue (1920 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Intrigue or The Martyrium is a 1920 German silent drama film directed by Paul L. Stein and starring Pola Negri and Eduard von Winterstein."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f1/Das_Martyrium_%281920%29_poster.jpg/330px-Das_Martyrium_%281920%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intrigue_(1920_film)","wikidata":"Q19796641"},{"title":"Intrigue (1942 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Intrigue (Spanish:Intriga) is a 1942 Spanish comedy mystery film directed by Antonio Román and starring Blanca de Silos and Manolo Morán. It is based on a novel by Wenceslao Fernández Flórez."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intrigue_(1942_film)","wikidata":"Q19572228"},{"title":"Intrigue (1947 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Intrigue is a 1947 American film noir crime film directed by Edwin L. Marin and starring George Raft, June Havoc and Helena Carter. Intrigue was intended to be the first of a number of films Raft made, with producer Sam Bischoff, for his own production company, Star Films. It was one of several movies Raft made with Marin."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0f/Intrigue_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wiki